  #sol-item(1, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    It is a plan, expressed in money or quantities, made before the period begins.
  ]

  #sol-item(2, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The comparison and the action are what make it control rather than planning.
  ]
  ]

  #sol-item(3, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Every other budget is driven by the volume the firm expects to sell.
  ]

  #sol-item(4, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    8,000 + 700 − 500 = 8,200 units.
  ]

  #sol-item(5, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    8,200 × 3 = 24,600 kg.
  ]

  #sol-item(6, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    24,600 + 1,300 − 1,000 = 24,900 kg.
  ]

  #sol-item(7, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    24,900 × 4 = ₦99,600.
  ]

  #sol-item(8, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    It is the complete plan, of which each functional budget is a part.
  ]

  #sol-item(9, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    It reconciles the departments' plans into one master budget.
  ]

  #sol-item(10, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Responsibility is the point: each centre has a manager answerable for its figures.
  ]

  #sol-item(11, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Each activity is re-justified, which is slower but exposes costs that have outlived their purpose.
  ]

  #sol-item(12, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Last year's figure is accepted as a base, so waste is built into every year.
  ]

  #sol-item(13, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    It is not adjusted for the actual activity, which is why control needs a flexible budget.
  ]

  #sol-item(14, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    It is flexed to what actually happened, so the variance measures control.
  ]

  #sol-item(15, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    20,000 + (3,000 × 6) = ₦38,000.
  ]

  #sol-item(16, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Actual 41,000 exceeds the flexed 38,000, so the firm spent more than it should have.
  ]

  #sol-item(17, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    It moves the result in the firm's favour.
  ]

  #sol-item(18, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    He negotiates the price and chooses the supplier.
  ]

  #sol-item(19, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    He controls how economically the material is used in the factory.
  ]

  #sol-item(20, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Depreciation is an allocation of past cost, not a movement of cash.
  ]

  #sol-item(21, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The cash budget records the money when it is received.
  ]

  #sol-item(22, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    15,000 + 80,000 − 70,000 = ₦25,000.
  ]

  #sol-item(23, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The balance before borrowing is −12,000, so the firm needs 17,000 to reach ₦5,000.
  ]

  #sol-item(24, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The negative figure is the finding, and it must be financed or managed.
  ]

  #sol-item(25, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Timing is the whole difference between the two statements.
  ]

  #sol-item(26, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Only the payment brings cash into the business.
  ]

  #sol-item(27, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    It protects the manager and costs the firm, and it is the classic behavioural weakness of budgeting.
  ]

  #sol-item(28, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    It improves acceptance, at the cost of speed and some slack.
  ]

  #sol-item(29, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The year is divided into months or quarters so that control can happen during it.
  ]

  #sol-item(30, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Both the volume and the value are needed to drive the other budgets.
  ]

  #sol-item(31, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The production volume is what determines the hours to be worked.
  ]

  #sol-item(32, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Contribution 5,000 × 15 = 75,000, less fixed 50,000 = ₦25,000.
  ]

  #sol-item(33, "A", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Production is driven by sales, so a shortfall in sales reduces the later budgets.
  ]

  #sol-item(34, "D", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    The sales plan becomes the production target and the buyer's order book.
  ]

  #sol-item(35, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    It shows the cash position month by month, and so the need to borrow.
  ]

  #sol-item(36, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    More hours than the standard for the same output is inefficiency.
  ]

  #sol-item(37, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    A capital purchase is a cash payment and part of the capital plan.
  ]

  #sol-item(38, "C", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    A target nobody believes in stops being a target.
  ]

  #sol-item(39, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
    Sales drives production, production drives materials, and all of them drive cash.
  ]

  #sol-item(40, "B", dense: true, pad: 0.0pt)[
